message.content:
Carob products fall in heading 1212: "Locust beans, seaweeds and other algae, sugar beet and sugar cane, fresh, chilled, frozen or dried, whether or not ground; fruit stones and kernels and other vegetable products... not elsewhere specified or included." Subheading 1212.92 covers locust beans (carob), and 1212.92.00 is the 8-digit level. The statistical suffix is 1212.92.0000 in the HTSUS.

Animal feed made of carob would otherwise go to 2309 (preparations of a kind used in animal feeding). However, 100% pure carob cubes are simply kibbled (cut up) carob pods, which remain in 1212. CBP rulings on kibbled carob have classified it in 1212.92.0000 (locust beans). I'll go with that.

{"hts_code": "1212.92.0000", "reason": "Pure kibbled carob pods remain locust beans (carob) of heading 1212, not a prepared animal feed of heading 2309, since they are merely cut or kibbled without any added ingredients."}
